WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.660
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.630
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.720
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.840
Your answers will...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.850
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.260
Even more...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.140
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.350
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:53.360
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.910
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.040
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.000
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.220
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.480
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.330
It's absurd.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:42.910
It's shameless.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:43.830
It's filthy.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.290
I can't believe this!

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.830
W-We're sorry...

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.250
But do you really understand?

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.590
Words don't mean a thing unless you mean them.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.470
I came here on business and I'm confronted with this...

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.470
For... extremely young boys and girls to be sharing the same room...

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.600
"Extremely young"?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.060
But...

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.180
...we didn't spend the whole night in the same room.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.770
Last night, we spent the whole time outside stargazing.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.110
We followed the Milky Way...

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.610
...and watched the sunrise.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.440
We felt revitalized and united.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.320
But after we'd cleared away our equipment...

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.080
...we all collapsed from exhaustion and fell asleep...

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.460
I don't even remember falling asleep-

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.580
No excuses!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.380
Since you've caused trouble, I'm forbidding you from holding any activities tonight.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.170
What?

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.630
You're also forbidden from using any of your equipment.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.180
N-No way!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.430
What is it? An enemy attack?

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.260
I will have some of my club members come and collect your equipment later.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.520
If you don't abide by this, I won't hesitate to use force.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.850
Make sure you keep that in mind.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.270
Fumin!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.900
I'm terribly sorry...

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:00.030
Don't say that. We were all dead tired.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.610
It was unavoidable.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.490
Still... Even though I was with you all...

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.540
I never knew that it was <i>that</i> bad for a boy and a girl to share the same room...

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.750
Is there really nothing we can do instead?

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.840
I didn't really manage to see much during our first stargazing session,

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.380
so yesterday was the first time I stargazed properly.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.090
It's a shame that I won't be able to see them again.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.640
Plus, I can be with him all night while stargazing.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.390
H-Hime-chan!

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.850
Hime-chan!

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.400
Thank you! I'm really happy!

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:40.400
But it's a pity to let these feelings of solidarity go to waste.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.190
Thank you!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.700
The camp is three days and four nights long.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.830
I can understand that we won't be able to stargaze if the weather's bad,

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.540
but in this perfect weather...

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.460
What's done is done!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.920
We will make up for this disgrace within our remaining time here!

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.130
Fumin's no demon.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.470
She's probably just testing us.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.510
And that's why, we're going to succeed!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.480
As a side note, according to my research, this is the Literature Club's schedule.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.980
Good job!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:13.940
It's nothing.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.060
Why?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.440
Just you wait, Fumin!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:20.900
Pardon us,

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.900
we're here to collect the equipment.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.530
No!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.120
And?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.080
What are those kids doing?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.290
I-I have no idea...

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.750
Maybe they're trying to show us that they're behaving.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.630
Geez, they're all idiots.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.010
Kotodzuka-senpai, you're too strict...

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.930
Listen, make sure you keep your distance from the Astronomy Club.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.050
Understood?

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.100
Yes!

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.060
Yes!

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.230
She's probably still worried despite that.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.850
Fumin!

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.650
She ignored us and walked away.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.650
That she did...

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:58.270
Yeah...

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.570
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.860
What we can do during the day is limited.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.240
We've been banned from using our equipment,

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.280
and there isn't a switch that converts day into night either...

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.160
But we've been forbidden from holding night activities, right?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.330
Yet the sky's so nice!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.170
Mihoshi!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.130
Alpha Cygni?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.170
[Note: Alpha Cygni/Deneb is the brightest star in the Cygnus constellation and one of the vertices of the Summer Triangle.]

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.130
Deneb.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.340
[Note: Alpha Lyrae/Vega is the brightest star in the Lyra constellation and forms the northern apex of the Summer Triangle.]

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.260
Alpha Lyrae?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:28.340
Vega.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.310
There's no point in working so hard.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.930
Let's ask Kotodzuka again later.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.020
Hime-chan.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.730
Alpha Scorpii?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.900
[Note: Alpha Scorpii/Antares is the brightest star in the Scorpion constellation and the 16th brightest star in the sky.]

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.270
Antares?

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:38.860
Correct.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.270
Me next!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.310
All right!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.520
Alpha Aquilae?

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:44.190
[Note: Alpha Aquilae/Altair is the brightest star in the Aquila constellation and one of the vertices of the Summer Triangle.]

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.150
Altair!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.610
Bingo!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.740
As expected from Yarai-kun.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.070
Yep.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.490
Well then... Let's have a break until four!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:54.580
Okay!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.510
Sayo-senpai, you're...

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:04.880
Yes?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.680
I'm so pale, I must look really ugly.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:10.800
Sorry.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.600
It's not that...

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.720
They just look a lot smaller when you've got clothes on, don't you think?

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.850
Take that!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.570
I-I can't change into my swimsuit...

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.490
Aren't you going to join them, Makita-san?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.490
I'm not...

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.320
Rather, I can't...

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.030
Excuse me.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:30.620
Huh?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.700
Hello.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.790
There are a lot of parasols here.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.660
May we join you?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.500
Sure, please do.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.380
Why are we playing Big-Two on the beach?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.050
I hear you've been having a hard time.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.420
Kotodzuka-senpai's furious.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.010
Oh yeah, now that you mention it,

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.470
why did Kotodzuka-senpai come by this morning?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.260
Oh, you mean she hasn't told you yet?

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.640
Ooyagi-kun?!

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:07.940
Kotodzuka-senpai!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.530
Oh, I'm sorry for disturbing you out of the blue.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.910
Um... it's about this...

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.950
Some Literature Club members told me...

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.790
...that you negotiated on our behalf to let us use the baths.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:27.840
Even though we managed to clean Souryukan, the bathroom still looks like hell...

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.260
We were just wondering what we should do about it.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.050
It's nothing.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.970
In the end, Muraoka-sensei was the one who made the decision.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:39.680
But even though you hate us, you still worry about us.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.810
That's what surprised me.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.440
Hey, let me tell you something,

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.150
I worry about everyone.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.240
Please stop talking as if you're the only ones who are being treated coldly.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.610
I will always be strict with those who cause trouble.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.160
Honestly, what you saw this morning... nothing happened.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.830
That's not the point.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.290
Just think of what impression you might be giving to others.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.960
There are people in school who think the Astronomy Club is trouble.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.260
One good example of that is that you don't have an official advisor.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.300
Being active at night can also lead to more problems than if you're just active during the day.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:15.390
I'm sorry.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.220
But you know, they're so beautiful.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.020
The stars.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.520
If only you saw them too...

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.780
I'm sure that you'd be able to see the star of words.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.200
The star of words?

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.160
That's...

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.210
Yoshinari! Izumi!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.710
And Makita-san too!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:46.880
Come on.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.300
Let us join your game of Big-Two.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.670
No!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.720
Stop it!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.010
Senpai!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.720
What's with you?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:04.350
Don't tell me that you wanna play with us instead.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:05.940
Let go of me!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.650
You bitch.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.490
Kotodzuka-senpai!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.450
I... didn't do... anything...

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.660
Saku-chan!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.460
Take this!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.630
Take this!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.500
Saku-chan!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.420
Ooyagi-kun!

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.250
Senpai!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.380
Saku-chan, are you all right?

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.720
Hey, are you all right?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.430
H-How uncool...

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:40.720
Are you all right?

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.140
Are you all right?!

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:42.810
Saku-chan!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:46.190
Hang in there, Ooyagi-kun!

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.020
Apple juice! Apple juice!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.690
My injury doesn't warrant a bandage...

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.070
I'm not sick either.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.320
His ring just cut me a little.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.610
More importantly, look.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.910
Kotodzuka-senpai said we could use their bath.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:04.500
Go.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.620
I'll follow once I've had a little rest.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.500
And after that, let's go and negotiate with her.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:11.290
Okay?

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:13.880
Okay.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.270
How uncool...

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.030
Everyone in the Astronomy Club looks up like that,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:39.860
from time to time.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.620
Are you checking the weather?

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.500
Thank you for earlier.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.870
For protecting my club members.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.120
No, it was nothing.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.840
I just slipped, that's all.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:54.090
Say...

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.970
What is a star of words?

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.720
To put it bluntly, I don't understand what's so good about stars.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.390
Although I might be getting the wrong impression from Akeno,

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:12.810
I get the impression that you all do club activities just so you can party at night.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.610
I feel like the two of us might share similar views,

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.200
so what is this star that you want to show me?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.950
I tried looking outside last night,

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.580
but I didn't see anything that impressive.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.130
That's-

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.840
It's fine if you don't say it.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.420
But in exchange,

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.470
show us what the Astronomy Club really does.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.560
What?!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.060
We've invited the Literature Club to one of our sessions?

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.020
Yeah.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.730
Well, she said she won't let us hold an activity tonight,

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:03.610
but if the Literature Club joins us, she said she'd okay it for tomorrow night.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.120
I just went ahead and agreed.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:07.280
What do you want to do?

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.330
Of course we'll do it!

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:09.080
We'll do it!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.290
It's the perfect opportunity to show them what we do!

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.670
But... how should we welcome them? What should we do?

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.130
You want some tea?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:17.920
No, no, no, no.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.420
Would you like some hot water?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.970
Calm down!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.590
I don't think this needs to be anything formal.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.760
All we need to do is show them what we do.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.850
We, the Astronomy Club, will be the host and-

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:39.360
Hey, everyone, did you call me, the charismatic host, Masashi?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.690
Stars, stars, stars,

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:40.990
So, what shall we do?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.030
It's best to show them the stars!

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.530
I'm sorry for being so noisy.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.120
What the hell?!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.780
Don't ignore me!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.160
Do you all lack a sense of humor?

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.170
The well known, Gin'rinbutai of Flames, sortie!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.170
[Note: Nickname of a squadron who used bicycles as their main form of transport during the Pacific War.]

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.550
Okay, let's check our schedule.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:10.390
Then,

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.930
Team Bravo, Team Charlie,

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.390
we're counting on you.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.270
Yes, Sir.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.150
Team Alpha, take care while acquiring the supplies.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.870
Lucky her.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.340
But you know, you're amazing, Saku-chan.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:40.590
What?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.460
How did you manage to ask Fumin?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.420
Are you two friends?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.340
I'd like to know more about that too!

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.680
It's not like we're friends or anything...

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.180
She just decided it as the Student Council President.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.440
She's thinking about us.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.270
The Astronomy Club.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.610
I see.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.860
I've been with Fumin since elementary school,

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.450
but we've never once stargazed together.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.240
She used to scold me for skipping summer camp in elementary school.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.870
In middle school, she used to keep an eye on me; I had a really hard time.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.580
She's the one who had a hard time.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:23.630
And finally, in the summer of our second high school year, she might finally be reconsidering things!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.840
Like financing a telescope for us.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.470
That's just a dream.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.180
The ogres will laugh at you for saying that, old lady.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.760
Let's do our best!

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.680
It's lonely when you say it alone,

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.400
but I love saying it when I'm with friends!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:55.450
Hey!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.500
Excuse me.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.580
May we borrow that tarp for tonight?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.000
Who are you?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:12.970
Oh my, aren't you the kids who were cleaning garbage off the beach yesterday?

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.310
Did you come all the way from Tokyo?

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:16.310
Yes.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:17.560
Is that so?

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:19.730
The tarp, right?

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:21.770
Sure, go ahead.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.030
Sayochin!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:31.780
Welcome back.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.530
It looks like they're preparing for something.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.040
Hey, are you making progress?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.410
Don't worry. I am.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.630
But I'm really looking forward to tonight.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.380
I wonder what they've planned.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.340
I'm sure you'll be able to see the star of words.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:15:59.770
Fumin!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.060
Beats me.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.980
I could never understand her.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.230
Senpai!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.410
We've received pamphlets from the Astronomy Club.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:14.780
Pamphlets?

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.580
Not only that, but they're handwritten too?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:21.870
Team Bravo!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.000
I mean, President!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.040
What's with this exceptionally large callous caused by writing too much?!

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.210
These pamphlets are all handwritten!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:28.880
All of them?!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.590
I... I couldn't find a photocopier,

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.050
but I've successfully made and delivered all 38 copies.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.520
I've even made you copies... too...

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.230
Take care of your health!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.740
It looks like he won't be able to do much tonight.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:56.320
Then, will you and Mihoshi-senpai take care of the explanations and coordination of the schedule?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:01.580
Hime-chan!

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:05.250
That's impossible!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.250
Absolutely impossible!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.830
Don't worry, Hime-chan.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.000
You managed to name a lot of the alpha stars as well as answer other questions.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.300
If we want to show them what we do,

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.970
we should also show them how our new members develop too!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.050
But...

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.510
Don't worry. Just remember Haruko-san's explanations.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.890
Kamona Planetarium!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.850
I can do some of the explanations too.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.020
Edogawa-kun!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.520
We'll get the freshmen to do the explanations,

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:31.190
and the others can answer any questions while they're guiding people.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.530
Let's do our best.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.870
Good evening, Literature Club members.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.700
I hope you all read your pamphlets.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.870
Everyone understands the rules, right?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.090
Anyone who isn't wearing any bug repellent, come this way please!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.010
It's almost time, right?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:04.220
Well, yes. I'll see how you guys do.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.060
In that case, we'll lead the way.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.650
Please make sure you follow us so that you don't get lost.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.410
W-Welcome!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:33.750
Today, we will guide you through some of our activities and tell you a little about the stars we observe.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.180
Stars...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.720
They are best observed on clear night skies;

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.760
in clear, unpolluted, dark places,

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:47.060
and moonless nights, such as tonight.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.520
We'll try our best to minimize your exposure to sources of artificial light,

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:55.400
so please take care not to look at any light sources.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:56.940
That's right...

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.740
That night, I never thought of that.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.200
Now then, please lie down.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:17.590
W-When you're looking for summer constellations, you should first look for the Summer Triangle.

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:23.180
Right above you, please search for Vega, from the constellation Lyra, which shines with a whitish-blue color.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:26.930
Is that it?

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.730
Below that is Altair from the Aquila constellation.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:34.770
Connect these two and the Deneb from the Cygnus constellation and you'll form a triangle.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:41.530
It said in the pamphlet that Vega is Orihime and Altair is Hikoboshi.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:41.530
[Note: Orihime and Hikoboshi are lovers that were separated and only allowed to meet once a year on the 7th day of the 7th month.]

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:47.080
If you follow the Milky Way and look towards your right, you will see the constellations Sagittarius and Scorpius.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.920
If you gaze at it, you might be able to see something faintly in the distant.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.550
That's where the center of the Milky Way is.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.430
Orihime and Hikoboshi.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:06.010
Is that the Summer Triangle?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.640
Which one's Altair?

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:09.930
Antares...

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:09.930
[Note: Antares is the name of a train that appears in Galaxy Rails 999.]

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.150
The reincarnation of Zeus?

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.150
[Note: They're referring to the constellations of Cygnus and Aquila.]

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.690
The Albireo Observatory.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.690
[Note: The name of an observatory in Albireo that appears in Galaxy Rail 999.]

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.780
In summer, the night.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.730
[Note: A famous poem by Sei Shounagon.]

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.320
[Note: A flock of magpies appear in the Orihime and Hikoboshi legend.]

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.320
A flock of magpies!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.820
I've thought up a story!

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.200
Orpheus' harp.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.200
[Note: The Lyra constellation.]

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:28.790
The half-human half-horse Chiron.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.410
You guys...

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.120
Did you read this pamphlet?

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.670
They're all checking the answers right now.

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.380
With the words and stories inside them.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:48.560
For most constellations, the story comes first and then the shape is given.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:53.060
That is why, even if you know how one looks, most don't make much sense.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:21:00.070
But if you learn even a few of the details, you can start to see their images on top of each other amongst the small lights.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.320
And the words connect one after the other...

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.490
Although, this depends on the person.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.450
The star of words, eh?

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.950
I think I understand you.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.540
It's like the hints are being collected.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.590
The words are pieces of a puzzle...

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.720
...that are waiting to be put back together.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:29.810
Words I've read and heard about are unconsciously collected inside of me...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.140
They've been waiting for me to gaze up like this.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:37.650
Fumin!

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.070
You've showed me something wonderful.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.990
It looks like I might need to reconsider.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.580
But I won't be giving you any extra financing.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:53.750
She saw straight through me!

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:57.170
Of course, I'll notify the school as well.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:58.750
Fumin!

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.460
You don't change.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:01.500
Neither do you.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:48.110
Next time on Sora no Manimani: Pleased to Meet You.

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:49.950
Oh, pleased to meet you too!
